ase case is highest single probability (40%).\n\n**B. Valuation Audit \u2014 PASS with caveat.** IV of $425 cross-checks with multiple methods (12-15x normalized EPS: $319\u2013$399; scenario-weighted DCF: $425; reverse DCF: current price requires 25% FCF CAGR 5-yr). Caveat: the quality transition justifies a higher multiple than historical; my 12-15x normalized range is *above* the 12-yr median P/E (~9x).\n\n**C. Bias Audit \u2014 PASS.** I am not anchored to the sell-side mean ($1,115). My Bear case is 30%, which aligns with base rates. I have not ignored the record FCF ($3.1B), the margin breakthrough, or the unprecedented forward visibility as arguments for higher valuation \u2014 I simply price them.\n\n**D. Consistency Audit \u2014 PASS.** I used SBC as an expense in adjusted FCF; I used GAAP-consistent margins; I did not mix Engine 4 (option-like) valuation with Engine 2 (cyclical) \u2014 the company has a real current-year earnings base; the optionality is already inside the revenue forecasts, not double-counted.\n\n**E. Narrative Audit \u2014 PASS.** The \"structural AI storage supercycle\" story is compelling; I have translated it into specific revenue/margin/FCF paths. I have not adopted the phrase \"large long-term potential\" without numbers.\n\n**F. Red Team Audit \u2014 PASS.** Section 9 present. Short thesis scored higher than long thesis. Killed arguments documented with revival criteria. Pre-mortem complete.\n\n**G. Data Integrity Audit \u2014 PARTIAL.** Primary filings (Sections 4\u20137) are internally consistent. Web-sourced narratives were cross-checked against filings:\n- Web brief revenue \"FY26 $10.06B\" contradicts filed $12.195B \u2192 **rejected**. Filings outrank.\n- Web brief \"short interest 0.0%\" contradicts pack's 4.06% short/float \u2192 **rejected**. Pack outranks.\n- Vendor total debt $3.858B vs my $3.898B sum (LT + current + leases): within 1% \u2014 good.\n- Q1 FY27 guidance $4.1B and EPS $7.30: confirmed across two independent