y and margin collapse; sold-out today invites capacity tomorrow.\n 3. Customer concentration: 88% of exabytes to data centers; BTO contracts lock\n    TODAY's scarcity pricing and reprice at the next renewal.\n 4. AI capex is itself a cyclical wave; a hyperscaler digestion pause hits the\n    highest-priced supplier first.\n 5. Reverse DCF: price implies $55\u201374B revenue (5\u20136\u00d7 today, 2\u20133\u00d7 the whole\n    industry) at 25% FCF margins \u2014 beyond base-rate plausibility.\n 6. Even the full bull case (20%/yr growth for 5 years, OM \u226530%) discounts to\n    ~$450\u2013550 \u2014 below the $802 price. The market has overshot its own best case.\n 7. 10-yr at 4.7% with hike risk: duration + cyclicality = double de-rating risk.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic combat (Long vs Short):\n Long: demand real (exabytes +39% YoY), supply consolidated (3 players), HAMR\n cost lead, sold-out through 2028, 20% growth target, $1.1T hyperscaler RPOs.\n Short: all of the above is POINT-IN-TIME scarcity; base rates say 30\u201340% odds of\n a \u226540% drawdown within 3 years; valuation requires best case at near-certainty.\n Score: Long 4/7, Short 6/7. Gap <2? No \u2014 gap = 2, at the threshold. Per\n framework, Long conviction is NOT upgraded; the gap supports avoiding, not\n fighting, the trend via naked shorts.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: no Hindenburg-class report held [Unconfirmed]; the\nstrongest published adversarial anchor is OptionsCafe (Mar-2026) fair value $475,\nbear $158 [Estimate]. GuruFocus GF Value $163, \"Significantly Overvalued\"\n[Estimate]. Both independent, both >2\u00d7 below current price \u2014 consistent with my\ncentral IV.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments (conditions to revive):\n \u2022 \"Sold out through 2028 = visibility\" \u2014 KILLED as a valuation input: it prices\n   sales, not the 2029+ cliff; revive if WD/Toshiba announce NO expansion AND\n   BTO renewals hold pricing into FY2029.\n \u2022 \"HAMR is a moat\" \u2014 KILLED beyond a 2-year lead; revive if 50TB+ drives keep\n   Seagate 12+ months ahead of every competitor AND NAND stays capacity-limited.\n \u2022 \"Multi-year contracts reduce cyclicality\" \u2014 KILLED (memory LTAs did not stop\n   the 2019/2023 crashes); revive if contracts extend >3 years with take-or-pay.\n \u2022 \"Management 20% target\" \u2014 KILLED as base case (same management guided revenue\n   down 37% in FY2023); revive only after 2+ years of \u226520% delivered WITH margins\n   \u226530%.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (condensed 37-point discipline)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n A. Methodology: Engine 2 selected with documented reason; no DCF-only, no\n    multiple-only, no TAM-only conclusion (three framework violations avoided).\n B. Valuation: discount rate derived (Rf 4.70% [Actual], ERP [Assumption], beta\n    2.10 [Aggregator]); every forecast driver sourced or tagged [Assumption];\n    periods beyond FY2027 explicitly flagged as unestablished and ranged in\n    scenarios; no silent decade-long trend extension. PASS.\n C. Bias: overconfidence audit \u2014 bull capped at 30% by the 1.5\u20132.0\u00d7 base-rate\n    rule; point estimates reported with 50%/80% CIs; base-case margins held 10pt\n    ABOVE historical median (pro-long bias) and IV still lands 2.4\u00d7 below price.\n    PASS.\n D. Consistency: no mixing of core vs optionality; no platform premium (no data);\n    non-GAAP vs GAAP basis differences flagged; time-points kept separate\n    (T0 2026-08-24; latest financials FY2026 / Q1 FY2027 guide). PASS.\n E. Narrative: management \"structural growth\" treated as a scenario, not fact.\n F. Red team: Section 9 completed; logic gap = 2 (threshold); short thesis\n    written from the same data. PASS.\n G. Data integrity: vendor P/B & ROE REJECTED (inconsistent with filings); pack\n    WC arithmetic rejected for DCF use (includes cash); R&D split [Unconfirmed];\n    segment data absent \u2014 no SOTP attempted; TTM series (2018) correctly\n    quarantined; fiscal-year series used instead. All discrepancies declared.\n No recalculation required after audit; no audit failure found.\n\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n Date: 2026-08-24 | T0 price $802.72 | Market cap $181.9B\n Central IV: $330 (50% CI $250\u2013460; 80% CI $150\u2013650) | MoS: \u2212143%\n Key assumptions logged: base OM fade 35%\u219224% (still 10pt > median); bull capped\n at 30% probability; WACC 12.5% (band 10\u201314.5%); FY2028+ revenue = management\n 20% target then deceleration.\n Red-team concerns logged: (1) momentum/squeeze can take price back toward $1,145\n against the thesis; (2) sell-side still +39% above price; (3) my margin-fade\n timing (FY2029) may be \u00b11 year wrong \u2014 handle via trigger thresholds, not\n conviction.\n Bias statement: I entered with no position; the pack's spectacular Q4 (NI +165%\n YoY) is seductive \u2014 the model was built to falsify the purchase, and it did.\n\nSECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25