ined.\n\n### 9-3 Adversarial Data\nNo major Hindenburg/activist short report captured in pack, but sell-side targets already show wide dispersion ($700\u2013$1,600), and the low target is below T0. Short interest rose 22% M/M.\n\n### 9-4 Killed Arguments\n- \"HAMR makes Seagate structurally different\": killed as a margin argument, but not as a growth argument; it can hold margins, but still cannot justify 58x FCF without absurd revenue growth.\n- \"Sold out through 2028 means no cycle\": killed; capacity allocation guarantees revenue, not the pricing that follows after 2028.\n- \"AI storage TAM is huge\": valid qualitatively, but until Seagate shows contractual visibility into CY2029+, it remains an untested assumption.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n- **A. Methodology Audit:** Pass \u2014 Engine 2 selected for cyclical archetype; DCF and reverse-DCF cross-checks performed.\n- **B. Valuation Audit:** Pass \u2014 no single-method conclusion; explicit forecast disclosed.\n- **C. Bias Audit:** Fail risk recognized \u2014 consensus is bullish; we specifically red-teamed with a short thesis.\n- **D. Consistency Audit:** Pass \u2014 all valuations use 22% tax rate, 11.5% WACC, 2.5% terminal growth.\n- **E. Narrative Audit:** Pass \u2014 \"AI supercycle\" not accepted at face value; tested against base rates.\n- **F. Red Team Audit:** Pass \u2014 short thesis completed before final opinion.\n- **G. Data Integrity Audit:** Pass with disclosures \u2014 R&D, segment data, and some debt components are marked [Unconfirmed] or [Assumption].\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n- **T0:** 2026-08-24, price $802.72\n- **Base IV:** ~$235 (probability-weighted)\n- **Key assumptions:** FY27 revenue $18B; FY28 revenue $21.6B; long-term EBIT margin 28%; WACC 11.5%; terminal growth 2.5%.\n- **Red-team concern:** The market is pricing a $70\u201390B revenue outcome; no visible contract or TAM evidence supports that in the data pack.\n- **Emotional check:** After a 48